    "summary": "Ventura high‑energy show with soaring Loser and epic Not Fade Away→Other One suite",
    "blurb": "The July 18 1982 Ventura performance delivers a blistering Loser, fiery Crazy Fingers and an unforgettable Not Fade Away → The Other One → Wharf Rat sequence. Jerry’s guitar soars while Phil lays down bass bombs throughout the set. Multiple excellent soundboard recordings capture the full show, making it essential listening for any 1982 era fan.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Ventura County Fairgrounds on a sun‑blazed July night is a high‑octane snapshot of the early‑’80s Dead. The first set rolls smoothly from New Minglewood Blues into a scorching Loser that sets the tone for an evening of relentless groove. Jerry’s lead work is nothing short of spectacular—his thundering solo on Loser and later lyrical flights through Crazy Fingers showcase a guitar voice that’s both fierce and melodic. Phil backs him with booming bass bombs, especially evident during the epic Not Fade Away → The Other One → Wharf Rat suite where his low‑end drives the band into psychedelic overdrive.\n\nThe second set keeps the momentum alive with a rapturous Franklin's Tower, a soulful Man Smart, Woman Smarter and a soaring Ship Of Fools. Brent’s keyboards add color without ever overwhelming the mix, while the twin drums of Mickey and Billy lock in tight, propelling the jams forward. The encore—Satisfaction into Brokedown Palace—offers a sweet, reflective close that balances the night’s intensity. With several pristine soundboard sources (the recommended Weinberg Sennheiser capture being the clearest), listeners can hear every nuance of this vibrant, beach‑side performance.",
